+# UI12 hand-back — 2026-10-06
+
+## Result
+
+The complete white Dock tile and signed B/I.A artwork now occupy 88% of the app-icon canvas. This leaves transparent space around the tile, so the application icon appears smaller beside other Dock apps without changing the artwork or enlarging its white border.
+
+The menu bar again uses Baton's bundled signed mark. It is cropped to its visible bounds, rendered at 3× menu resolution in a theme-aware gray gradient, and retains the neutral decision dot. The app and Dock keep their original burgundy and black. Light and Graphite PNGs, with and without the decision badge, were inspected.
+
+## Files
+
+- `app/Sources/BatonUI/Components/BrandMark.swift`
+- `app/Sources/BatonUI/Screens/Popover/PopoverView.swift`
+- `app/Tests/BatonUITests/BrandTests.swift`
+- `docs/plan/STATUS.md`
+- `docs/plan/track-d-app.md`
+- `docs/plan/reports/UI12-2026-10-06.md`
+
+## Checks
+
+Engine command: `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`.
+
+```text
+...........................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................
+----------------------------------------------------------------------
+Ran 379 tests in 2.398s
+
+OK
+```
+
+App build: `cd app && swift build` with `CLANG_MODULE_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/baton-clang-cache`, `SWIFT_MODULECACHE_PATH=/tmp/baton-swift-cache`, installed SDK26.5 and TestingMacros flags, and `--disable-sandbox`.
+
+```text
+Build complete! (4.00 secs)
+```
+
+App tests: `cd app && swift test` with the same cache, SDK, TestingMacros and sandbox flags.
+
+```text
+✔ Test run with 78 tests in 11 suites passed after 7.574 seconds.
+✔ Test run with 18 tests in 5 suites passed after 0.477 seconds.
+```
+
+Layer rule: `grep -rnE '^(from|import) .*(adapters|ledger)' baton/domain baton/ports baton/services` emitted no output (exit 1). Core tool-name rule: `grep -rniE 'claude|codex|opencode|cursor' baton/ports baton/services tests/adapters/suite.py` emitted no output (exit 1). UI12 adds no user-facing sentences. `git diff --check` emitted no output (exit 0). The shared tree contains earlier uncommitted package work; the UI12 delta is restricted to the files listed above.
+
+The first unsandboxed Swift build attempt without writable module caches failed while compiling the manifest. The required cache and installed-SDK flags produced the successful build and tests above.
+
+## Review challenge
+
+Pixel tests bound the Dock artwork and verify its signature, transparent outer canvas, white tile and retained burgundy pixels. The menu test now checks a fixed silhouette pattern and the detached I.A region, which a generic chain symbol cannot satisfy. Every near-opaque menu pixel is checked for grayscale values in both themes and badge states. The previous UI11 snapshots and the new UI12 PNGs were visually compared; the whole tile is smaller and the menu shape now matches the logo.
+
+Independent review initially found two issues: cropping the 1254×1254 source on every menu label refresh, and a test that compared two renders of the same component. The source and cropped images are now cached on the main actor, and the test asserts independent alpha geometry. The reviewer rechecked the diff and found no remaining blocker. The 19-point I.A signature is tiny in the PNG, and actual system menu-bar pixels were not captured. No engine behavior or real chat was changed.
+
+## Native fixture
+
+Only the approved `/private/tmp/BatonFixture.app` was refreshed. The prior fixture was closed through its own Quit confirmation; its executable and both SwiftPM resource bundles were copied from the successful build, then the temporary app was signed and verified:
+
+```text
+/private/tmp/BatonFixture.app: valid on disk
+/private/tmp/BatonFixture.app: satisfies its Designated Requirement
+```
+
+LaunchServices accepted `open -n /private/tmp/BatonFixture.app --args --review-window`. The new process remained running after launch, no new Baton crash report appeared, and Computer Use confirmed the current Baton window is visible. The menu and Dock image pixels were inspected in the generated PNGs; no real coding app or chat was touched.
+
+## Commit
+
+Git metadata is read-only in this environment. `docs/plan/reports/patches/UI12.patch` applies after UI11 and reproduces the scoped files. The exact paths and commit message are in the UI12 Ready to commit entry in STATUS.md. No commit or push was attempted.
